            <ArticleTitle>Postauricular abscess leading to internal jugular vein thrombosis: a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>258, 260</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Thrombosis of the internal jugular vein (IJV) is uncommon. It usually responds to conservative medical treatment. We describe a case of IJV thrombosis in a 31-year-old man. The patient was successfully treated with IJV ligation after conservative therapy had failed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
